{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task SE-PE-01 involves implementing `grammar_guided_node_reduction` through `solve(case)`. Let me understand the requirements:\n\n1. We have a parse tree with nodes, each having: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility\n2. We need to reduce the tree by removing nodes while preserving required symbols\n3. Rules:\n   - Never remove root, a required symbol node, or a node with retained children\n   - Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n   - Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\n   - Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n   - Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\n\nLet me think about the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure\n2. Process nodes from deepest to shallowest (for equal depth, use node ID as tie-break)\n3. For each node (deepest first), check if it can be removed:\n   - It must be `removable: true`\n   - It must not have retained children\n   - After removal, all required symbols must still be represented\n4. If removable, remove it (add to removed list)\n5. Return retained_node_ids (sorted) and removed_node_ids (in removal order)\n\nLet me trace through case 000:\n- Nodes:\n  - root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root\n  - n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1\n  - n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2\n  - n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0\n  - n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n  - n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n  - n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcessing order (deepest first, then by node ID):\n- Depth 2: n4 (s1), n5 (s2), n6 (s0)\n- Depth 1: n1 (s1), n2 (s2), n3 (s0)\n- Depth 0: root\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1):\n- Has no children (no nodes have parent=n4)\n- If we remove n4: remaining nodes would be root, n1, n2, n3, n5, n6\n- Symbols still present: root (root), s1 (n1), s2 (n2), s0 (n3), s2 (n5), s0 (n6)\n- Required symbols: root ✓, s1 ✓ (n1 has s1)\n- Can remove n4 ✓\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2):\n- removable=false, skip\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0):\n- Has no children\n- If we remove n6: remaining nodes would be root, n1, n2, n3, n5 (n4 already removed)\n- Symbols: root, s1 (n1), s2 (n2), s0 (n3), s2 (n5)\n- Required: root ✓, s1 ✓\n- Can remove n6 ✓\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- Skip (not removable)\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2):\n- Has children? n4 is already removed. No retained children.\n- If we remove n2: remaining nodes would be root, n1, n3, n5\n- Symbols: root, s1 (n1), s0 (n3), s2 (n5)\n- Required: root ✓, s1 ✓\n- Can remove n2 ✓\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- Skip\n\nProcess root (depth=0, removable=false):\n- Skip\n\nSo removed: [n4, n6, n2] (in order of processing)\nRetained: [root, n1, n3, n5]\n\nReturn:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"] (actual removal order)\n- retained_node_ids: [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"] (sorted)\n\nWait, \"sorted\" - how? Alphabetically? By... let me re-read: \"Return sorted retained IDs\". I'll assume lexicographic sort for string IDs.\n\nLexicographic sort of [\"root\", \"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\"]: \n- \"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"\n\nNow let me implement the solve function:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build node lookup and children map\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track which nodes are currently retained\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    # Sort nodes: deepest first, then by node ID (stable tie-break)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if has retained children\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if all required symbols remain after tentative removal\n        # Current retained symbols minus this node's symbol\n        # We need to check if required symbols are still covered\n        retained_without = retained - {nid}\n        symbols_without = set(node_map[nid2][\"symbol\"] for nid2 in retained_without)\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_without):\n            retained.remove(nid)\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nWait, I need to be careful. The children map should only consider children that are currently retained. Let me re-check.\n\n\"Never remove ... a node with retained children\" - so when checking if a node can be removed, check if any of its direct children are still retained.\n\nThe logic seems correct. Let me trace through again more carefully.\n\nActually wait - processing order. \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes. Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\"\n\nSo we sort by (-depth, node_id). Let me verify the node IDs are strings and sorted lexicographically. IDs are \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", etc.\n\nFor case 000, sorted order:\n- Depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (lexicographic: n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6)\n- Depth 1: n1, n2, n3 (lexicographic: n1 \u003c n2 \u003c n3)\n- Depth 0: root\n\nThis matches what I traced earlier. The implementation looks correct.\n\nLet me double check the children tracking. When processing n2 at depth 1, n4 (its child) has already been removed from `retained`. So `any(c in retained for c in children[\"n2\"])` = `any(c in retained for c in [\"n4\"])` = `\"n4\" in retained` = False (since n4 was removed). Good.\n\nNow let me write the final implementation as a JSON string.\n\nThe response needs to be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source.\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        retained_without = retained - {nid}\n        symbols_without = set(node_map[nid2][\"symbol\"] for nid2 in retained_without)\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_without):\n            retained.remove(nid)\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks good. Let me now format it as the required JSON response.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    retained = set(n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    # Deepest first; stable tie-break by node ID (lexicographic)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Hard constraint: must be marked removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Hard constraint: no retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Hard constraint: all required symbols still covered after tentative removal\\n        retained_without = retained - {nid}\\n        symbols_without = {node_map[nid2][\\\"symbol\\\"] for nid2 in retained_without}\\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(symbols_without):\\n            continue\\n\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01kFFGRDVDK1ckNFj3YXxX6P","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2397},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2397,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":63,"output_tokens":2562,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2167},"service_tier":"standard"}}